Z||000000||DXR_DAD||08-02-99||11:02 PM||||I have read other posts: fan under rear grills, fan switch, over the roof scoops, side scoops. So what is up?, whats the best way to keep it cool?  It seems to be damm hot back there and with the addition of headers would that make it hotter? and is this ~one~ of the reasons that the exhaust manifolds crack? DXR_WILL has forced me to repair my manifold leaks. And this heat thing has come up time and time again.
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||08-03-99||12:50 AM||||P.S.  What about those silver tubes and the fan in the trunk? The fans in the grills, is this a exhaust fan to pull the hot air out?, or a fan to pull outside air in. I have also<br>seen small hood scoops on the rear deck lid of some fieros like to old style mustangs, do these hood scoops help any?
Z||000002||Bruce||08-03-99||10:00 AM||||Since I installed the K&N air filter, my engine seems to run alot cooler. But, I live on the Northern California coast and don't see the temperatures some of you guys do. I think the basics are always important: check the coolant and oil on a regular basis, and change those two according to the owners' manual. 
Z||000003||ratt||08-03-99||02:07 PM||||The vents were designed to allow air to flow out of the engine compartment so I would only consider mods that would enhance this.  I combined my 86 vents with the honeycomb screen from an 85 which allowed a fair amount more hot air to escape (the screen just keeps flammables out such as pine needles etc.) Don't use the 85 vents as the casting design is much more restrictive than the newer models.  I drive my fiero in the winter & have noticed that the driver side vent flows more air than the passenger side by the amount of snow & ice that melts off the ends of my spoiler.  I figure this is due to the battery being under the passenger<br>vent.  If you were to relocate the battery to the front it may allow even better air flow (a california club offers a neat looking battery box for mounting the battery under the spare).  The mustang type scoop would probably help even more as well as adding side scoops to pipe more cool air through the engine compartment.  You could also invest in an exhaust system which drops the muffler & just uses resonator tips.
Z||000004||Dave85||08-04-99||10:25 PM||||I have an '85 GT and I just went to full synthetic oil and Prolong. WOW... What a difference!!!
